ds the nearest binder and, when the binder's type is unknown, falls back to the file-wide map and then the import (its docstring at 1620-1630 says letting untyped binders shadow was deliberately rejected -- read that before changing it). A Kotlin fixture with a parameter `Files: Any` did NOT reproduce (typed `Any` routes to external); the untyped-local shape was not tried.\n\nDIRECTION: false positive in the module slot (a catalogued class's row for an object that is not one). Java locals are conventionally lowerCamel, so the shape is probably rarer than in Python; NOT MEASURED."  # d9b8
